& [PreservedQuestion] is exact
  + schemars has distinct Deserialize and Serialize contracts and includes contract in its schema UID
  + prepare, run, and verify requests are decoded and therefore require deserialization schemas
  + base and preparation responses are emitted and therefore require serialization schemas
  + PreparedRunRequest crosses the direction boundary as preparation output and run input
  + decide how canonical documents, definition identities, fingerprints, residuals, and bundles preserve direction without duplicating semantic type identity

& [RequiredOutcome] is bounded
  + direction must be explicit in every schema document and definition fingerprint
  + input and output definitions must never be silently interchanged
  + equal normalized definitions across directions may be reported equal but not presumed equal
  + compatibility must compare within the same direction and report cross-direction reuse separately
  - never: generate schemas, add a dependency, alter public forms, or activate CPMS-I02 from source preservation alone

& [AttributionLimit] is explicit
  + user authorized continued SJS-governed Cantor work
  + exact direction distinction was discovered by the manager from pinned library source

